      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are actually right, but then Gerrit misbehave anyway, because users are NOT allowed to have two emails with different local part cases.\n\nExample:\n1. Create an empty Gerrit with admin having email admin@mycompany.com\n2. Try to add a secondary email having ADMIN@mycompany.com\n\nGerrit *must* allow that, isn\u0027t it? Instead we get:\n```\nAn error occurred\nError 409 (Conflict): email exists\n\nEndpoint: /account/self/emails/*\n```",
      "parentUuid": "ee8213f2_4e2b0343",
